WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:08.080
Dune is one of the most famous sci fi books&nbsp;
ever. The story of Paul Atreides’ rise to power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:14.800
is widely read, and been made into movies and&nbsp;
TV shows. But this book is not the whole story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.840
of Dune – Frank Herbert wrote six Dune&nbsp;
books, and it’s only in these sequels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:27.040
that the true meaning of Dune is revealed.
The Dune sequel books get weird. Paul’s son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:34.640
transforms into a worm god and rules for thousands&nbsp;
of years. Duncan Idaho gets resurrected hundreds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:42.160
of times. There's an invasion by dominatrixes&nbsp;
from space, and genetically modified cat-people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:50.960
and chairs made out of living dogs. And each book&nbsp;
is full of secret plots and abstract philosophical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:59.120
ideas. It would take many videos to fully explore&nbsp;
these books. So first, what’s the basic story?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:06.800
What happens in Frank Herbert’s six Dune books?
In Book 1, House Atreides takes over the desert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:13.040
planet Arrakis, land of sandworms and spice.&nbsp;
But they’re attacked by the Harkonnens and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.800
the Emperor. Paul Atreides unlocks a powerful&nbsp;
[prescient] mind that can see into the future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:24.880
He becomes a religious leader to the native&nbsp;
Fremen, and falls in love with Chani. He defeats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:30.320
the Harkonnens and defeats Emperor Shaddam,&nbsp;
and Paul becomes Emperor of the Universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:37.360
So Book 1 seems to be a classic story of a&nbsp;
hero fulfilling his destiny and defeating evil.&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:45.920
But in Book 2, Dune Messiah, Paul being Emperor&nbsp;
is a disaster. The Fremen kill billions of people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:54.240
in a holy war. And Paul can’t stop the violence –&nbsp;
his religion is out of his control. A conspiracy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:01.760
of powerful people plot to destroy Paul – led by&nbsp;
Gaius Mohiam, and by Paul's wife Princess Irulan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:07.120
with a Spacing Guild Navigator [Steersman], and&nbsp;
a Tleilaxu Face Dancer, and Paul’s own Fremen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:14.960
High Priest. These guys have an elaborate plan to&nbsp;
destroy Paul using a cryptic dwarf called Bijaz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:21.680
who manipulates a resurrected version of Duncan&nbsp;
Idaho who is now a Mentat [cyborg] philosopher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:28.160
with robot eyes. Paul knows there’s a plot against&nbsp;
him. But he allows some of their plan to happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:35.200
anyway because he's afraid of even worse possible&nbsp;
futures happening instead. Seeing the future is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:42.640
curse, it’s a trap that takes away Paul's free&nbsp;
will. Paul gets blinded by a nuclear weapon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:50.560
and relies on his visions to see – like Neo in&nbsp;
The Matrix 3. Chani dies giving birth to twins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:58.240
Leto the Second and Ghanima. Paul wants to escape&nbsp;
his grief and politics and destiny so he walks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:05.520
into the desert to die. So in Dune Messiah, Paul's&nbsp;
rise as a heroic leader turns out to’ve been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:12.880
a terrible mistake. He loses everything he&nbsp;
loves, and gets billions of people killed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:19.120
The message is that religious and political&nbsp;
leaders are dangerous. Blindly following a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:28.640
messiah or a vision or plan can lead to disaster.
Book 3 is Children of Dune. Paul's sister Alia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:34.960
rules the universe on behalf of young Leto&nbsp;
and Ghanima. But Alia’s mind gets possessed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:41.920
taken over by the memory of the Baron Vladimir&nbsp;
Harkonnen. Turns out that the Baron was Alia and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:48.880
Paul’s grandfather, and his personality corrupts&nbsp;
Alia’s mind and leads her government into decline.&nbsp;

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:55.680
It turns out that changing the environment of&nbsp;
Arrakis to have water and plants is a disaster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:01.760
because without desert, there’s no sandworms and&nbsp;
no spice, and Fremen desert culture starts to die.&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:08.720
Paul turns out to be alive still as a&nbsp;
mysterious desert preacher. He criticises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:14.400
the Atreides religion and government, but ends&nbsp;
up getting stabbed to death by his own priests.&nbsp;

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:22.160
Wensicia Corrino, the daughter of the old Emperor&nbsp;
Shaddam, plots against the Atreides. She tries to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:28.800
kill Leto and Ghanima with Laza tigers. So&nbsp;
Leto fakes his own death and gets super high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:35.520
in the desert to unlock his mind. And Leto sees&nbsp;
a possible future that could save humanity from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:43.200
extinction, a plan called the Golden Path. Leto&nbsp;
transforms his own body so he'll become part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:49.120
sandworm and will rule the universe for&nbsp;
thousands of years. Jessica deals with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:53.280
Corrinos by converting their heir to the Bene&nbsp;
Gesserit, and marrying him to Ghanima. Alia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.280 --> 00:05:00.560
kills herself to kill the Baron within her. And&nbsp;
worm boy Leto becomes Emperor. So Leto’s plan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:07.280
will apparently save the human species. But to&nbsp;
be the saviour he has to give up his humanity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:14.320
and become a monstrous tyrant. Dune&nbsp;
rejects the heroic messiah Paul and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:22.640
instead turns to a darker more complicated leader.
Book 4 is God Emperor of Dune, set thousands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:29.920
years after the previous books. Leto rules the&nbsp;
universe with an iron fist. His plan, the Golden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:36.640
Path, is to oppress humanity for thousands of&nbsp;
years, to teach the species to want freedom to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:44.080
grow stronger, and to think for ourselves. Leto&nbsp;
also breeds the Atreides bloodline to create Siona&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:51.040
Atreides. Siona has a special gene that makes her&nbsp;
invisible to people who can see the future. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:56.960
Siona’s genes will free humanity from the control&nbsp;
of prescient people [like Leto and Paul]. Leto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:04.240
falls in love with a woman called Hwi. Trapped in&nbsp;
his monstrous worm body, Leto is tormented by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:11.680
loss of his humanity, his tragic self-sacrifice&nbsp;
to save the species. Over the centuries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:19.200
Leto resurrects Duncan Idaho over and over, and&nbsp;
he allows Duncan and Siona to rebel against him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:26.240
He teaches Duncan and Siona so they grow strong&nbsp;
enough to eventually destroy him. In the end they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:36.000
kill Leto by using the blind obedience of Nayla,&nbsp;
a fanatic of Leto’s religion. Leto’s dying body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:42.960
rejuvenates the sandworms and spice on Arrakis,&nbsp;
and humanity is finally freed from his control.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:49.840
After millennia of oppression, humanity bursts&nbsp;
out across the universe in The Scattering, a mass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:57.840
migration into space. Humanity expands and evolves&nbsp;
to save it from stagnation and extinction – just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:05.280
as Leto planned. His Golden Path gives&nbsp;
humanity a universe of infinite possibilities.&nbsp;

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:11.840
Book 5, Heretics of Dune, is set another&nbsp;
thousand years in the future. The Bene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:17.600
Gesserit control much of the Old Empire,&nbsp;
but a new threat comes from the Scattering.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:24.640
The Honoured Matres are a wild offshoot from&nbsp;
the Bene Gesserit who use sex to enslave people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:30.800
The Bene Gesserit train a girl called Sheeana who&nbsp;
can control sandworms, and they hope to breed her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:37.760
with a new resurrected Duncan Idaho, and to use&nbsp;
her as a religious force to control people. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:44.080
there’s also a plot by the Tleilaxu, a bunch of&nbsp;
religious genetic scientists who look like creepy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:51.040
grey elves. The Tleilaxu secretly modified this&nbsp;
new Duncan, giving him special sex powers – which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:57.280
terrifies the Honoured Matres. Bene Gesserit&nbsp;
leader Taraza uses Duncan to lure the Honoured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:03.600
Matres into destroying the planet Arrakis. Cause&nbsp;
by killing the planet’s sandworms, they destroy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:10.000
the remnants of Emperor Leto’s consciousness&nbsp;
and end his influence on the universe. The Bene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:15.280
Gesserit take the last sandworm to make spice on&nbsp;
their own planet called Chapterhouse. Taraza is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:23.040
helped by Miles Teg, a legendary Atreides soldier&nbsp;
who sacrifices himself and dies on Arrakis.&nbsp;

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:30.560
In Book 6, Chapterhouse: Dune, the Honoured Matres&nbsp;
rampage across the Empire, hunting to exterminate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:35.440
the Bene Gesserit. The Bene Gesserit go&nbsp;
into hiding on the planet Chapterhouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:40.080
under the leadership of Darwi Odrade, an&nbsp;
unusually rebellious and emotional Reverend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:46.800
Mother who wants her Sisterhood to change and&nbsp;
evolve to survive this crisis. Odrade creates a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:53.280
young clone of Miles Teg who is her father.&nbsp;
And she trains a captured Honoured Matre,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.280 --> 00:09:00.720
Murbella, to be a Bene Gesserit. Murbella and&nbsp;
Duncan fall in love. Teg leads an attack on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:08.320
Honoured Matres. But the Matres defeat Teg with a&nbsp;
secret weapon, and they kill Odrade. So Murbella&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:14.480
infiltrates and takes over the Honoured Matres&nbsp;
from within. Then she merges the Honoured Matres&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:22.720
with the Bene Gesserit, assimilating to create&nbsp;
a new stronger Sisterhood. Murbella has changed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:27.840
so much that Duncan decides to leave her.&nbsp;
He and Sheeana steal a spaceship and escape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:35.760
along with the last living Tleilaxu Master, and a&nbsp;
secret group of Jewish people and some sandworms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:43.920
and a Van Gogh painting. Together they start a&nbsp;
new journey, free in the infinite universe. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:51.280
final chapter, we see a mysterious elderly couple&nbsp;
called Daniel and Marty. These two are apparently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:56.160
advanced Face Dancers from the Scattering&nbsp;
who escaped the control of the Tleilaxu.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.160 --> 00:10:02.960
But Daniel and Marty also seem to represent&nbsp;
the author Frank Herbert and his wife Beverly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:09.440
As they work in their garden, they break the&nbsp;
fourth wall, chatting about Dune’s characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:15.680
and the unfinished plotlines like the Tleilaxu.&nbsp;
They admit that the characters got away from them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:24.400
beyond of the author’s control. The book ends with&nbsp;
a loving tribute to Bev, who died the previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:32.640
year. The year after publication, Frank died.
So Frank never wrote a neat final conclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:39.440
to the Dune series. But this open-ended last&nbsp;
chapter fit the central themes of Dune – the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:45.840
characters get freedom and self-determination,&nbsp;
not even the author controls them any more.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:52.320
And Daniel and Marty in their garden show the&nbsp;
simple human warmth that is the emotional heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.320 --> 00:11:00.080
of Dune. Dune was never really about the plot&nbsp;
as much as it’s about the ideas. A philosophy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:07.680
of the mind, of thinking, politics, technology,&nbsp;
of how to live in a chaotic universe. So we’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:13.840
making a video called The Philosophy of Dune,&nbsp;
exploring the themes and big ideas of the series.&nbsp;

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:18.800
We're also gonna cover the new Game of&nbsp;
Thrones TV show, House of the Dragon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:25.200
which is based on a book called Fire &amp; Blood.
